# Demo UI — External CSS Only

When editing `docs/demo/`, keep presentation CSS in `.css` files, not in markup or JS templates.

## Do

- Link stylesheets with `<link rel="stylesheet" href="...">`
- Add rules to the nearest existing sheet (see map below) or a new co-located `.css`
- Prefer semantic classes (`.fs-steps-hint`, `.nr-meta--top`) over inline attributes
- Run `./scripts/validate-demo-external-css.sh` before marking the task done

## Do not

- `<style>...</style>` blocks in HTML
- `style="..."` on HTML elements or in JS template strings
- Duplicating the same rules across multiple HTML files

## Stylesheet map

| Area | Files |
|---|---|
| FlowStory (architecture + scenarios) | `shared/vendor/style.css`, `shared/demo.css` |
| Launcher | `v1/narrative.css`, `index.css` |
| Narrative v1 | `v1/narrative.css` |
| Narrative v2 embed | `v2/baseline-embed.css`, `v2/narrative-v2.css`, … |

## Allowed exceptions

| Case | Example |
|---|---|
| SVG assets | `docs/demo/shared/assets/**` |
| Vendored libs | `docs/demo/shared/vendor/**` |
| Runtime JS | `element.style.display = "flex"` (property, not HTML attribute) |

## Fix pattern

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<style>.panel { padding: 8px; }</style>
<button style="color:#79c0ff">Loop</button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./shared/demo.css">
<button id="fs-loop">Loop</button>
```

```css
/* shared/demo.css */
#fs-loop { border-color: #79c0ff; color: #79c0ff; }
```

For refactor or audit workflows, use the `demo-external-css` skill.
